doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23175063
keywords:
  - Parkinson's disease
  - evidence grading
  - evidence synthesis
  - protocol
  - patient information
abstract: >-
  A versioned rulebook for grading published evidence against the questions
  people with Parkinson's ask. Each rule has an id. A study and a claim produce
  a Priority grade that ranks the strength of the evidence for the claim as
  written. Grades are derived from the rules, never stored, and any rule change
  bumps the version. Draft, not clinician reviewed, not medical advice.
